<h3 id="Machines">Machines</h3>

<p>Machines are used by Pilots to extract oil from the ground and pipe it to a landing pad where it is packaged into barrels for helicopter extraction.  Machines can only be deployed from the city where they are mined.  Adjacent to this city is a field where underground oil is plentiful but acid rain eats at everything.  Once a machine is deployed, it will work automatically at its designed purpose until the rain eats it away.  Other players deploy their machines at the same field and you may find that not all the oil you extract ends up in your inventory.  </p>

<p>There are many different models of machines all categorized into these types:<p>
<ul>
<li>Pump: Pumps oil from the ground into the pump's hex.  There's no limit to the oil underground.  Oil will collect at the pump unless it's piped elsewhere.</li>
<li>Pipe: Moves oil from one hex to another.</li>
<li>Pad: Packs oil into barrels.  When a barrel is full, the owner of the pad can retrieve the barrel.  Unfinished barrels persist through machine changes. </li>
<li>Pelter: Throws rocks at a neighboring machine, reducing its lifespan.  </li>
<li>Power: Powers an adjacent machine.  This means it adds its own kw to the machine it is facing (including other powers). </li>
</ul>

<p>Machines must be deployed no more than N+1 hexes away from the center where N is the distance of the closest empty spot.  Within this area you can place machines on any blue empty spot or top of your own deployed machines replacing them.  Once deployed, machines cannot be moved or rotated.</p>

<p>Occasionally oil will seep up through the ground on its own.  If this happens, nobody will be able to deploy on the hex.  This is fixed by piping the oil away until there is less than 2000L.  </P>

<h3 id="Rules">Rules</h3>

<p>There are only two rules in this game: 1) one account per person and 2) no trading in-game goods/gold for out-of-game goods/cash.</p>

<p>1. <b>Each person is only allowed exactly one account per game server.</b>  This encompasses a few different activities.  The intent of the rule is that one person cannot benefit from using many accounts and one account cannot benefit from using many people.  Should any of the following occur, the offender(s) will be found in violation of this rule:</p>

<ul>
<li>a. Someone logs into, or uses for any purpose, more than one account per game server. *</li>
<li>b. Someone gives their password or allows access or use of their account by another person.</li>
<li>c. Someone asks for another's password or otherwise encourages their password to be shared.</li>
<li>d. One account transfers a significant portion of its wealth to another ("significant" intentionally left undefined).</li>
</ul>

<p>Should any accounts be involved in the above activities, they are subject to being reset.  When an account is "reset," all of its things, melds, gold, credits, mines and any other in-game valuables are deleted.  </p>

<p>* The only exception to part a. is when someone wants to start over with a new account.  If a person does start over, they must not ever access the old account  after starting the new one or use it in any way.  They must also avoid parts b-d above.</p>

<p>It's perfectly fine for one person to have an account on each game server.</p>

<p>2. <b>No selling in-game valuables for out-of-game valuables.</b>  This sort of thing encourages gold farming and promotes a pay-to-win environment.  Should any of the following occur, the offenders will be found in violation of this rule:</p>

<ul>
<li>a. Someone offers their account or any in-game property in exchange for credits, out-of-game money, goods or services.
<li>b. Someone offers credits, out-of-game money, goods or services in exchange for an account or their in-game property.
<li>c. Someone offers goods/gold on one game server in exchange for goods/gold on another game server.   
<li>d. Someone facilitates a. b. or c. in any way.
</ul>

<p>Enforcement of these rules is accomplished by an automated script and also by players reporting illegal behavior.  It is not enforced by IP address.  Any number of accounts following the above rules can use the same IP address without any problems.</p>

<h3 id="Privacy">Privacy Policy</h3>

<p>Entering your email on the account page is optional.  The only way the email is used is on the password recovery page.  It is not required but highly recommended because it's the only way that you can identify yourself should you ever forget your password.</p>

<p>To optimize marketing efforts, Minethings servers will send new miners' IP to Google Adwords and trigger their browser to store a cookie.  This is so that those players can be shown extra ads reminding them that they have a robot who worked very hard to find things while they were gone and to please recharge their battery.  This marketing effort automatically ends either when the miner does return for a recharge or after some time has passed.  It's designed only to recruit more players and for no other purpose.  No personal information is sent to Google as a result.  You can opt out of this by visiting <a href="http://www.google.com/settings/ads">Google's Ad Settings</a>.</p>

